# What NEVER leaves this machine.
#
# ==================== THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore, IT DOES NOT EXTEND IT ====================
# Once a .vercelignore exists, Vercel stops consulting .gitignore -- so anything that was
# excluded only by .gitignore has to be repeated here. Two of the entries below are the
# reason this file exists at all rather than being left to the default:
#
#   .recordings/  6.5MB of recorded calls. Strangers describing their homes and leaving
#                 phone numbers. It belongs in a private blob store, not in a build context.
#   .cache/       49MB of Census bulk files. Re-fetchable, and nothing at runtime reads it.
# ============================================================================================

.env
.env.local

.recordings/
.recordings-smoke/
.cache/

node_modules/
.next/
.next-build/
dist/
.vercel/

.git/
*.log
.playwright-mcp/
*.png

# Tests do not run in the build, and the e2e suite would need a database.
# NOTE: __fixtures__ directories are deliberately NOT excluded -- the provider seam loads
# them whenever LIVE_CALLS_ENABLED is not exactly "true", which includes any misconfigured
# deploy. Dropping them would turn a $0 fallback into a crash.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.e2e.test.ts
